+## Delivery policy
+
+Each channel stores a human-readable `purpose`, a `fanout_policy`, and an optional
+`coordinator_peer_id`. These fields guide prompt activation for unaddressed public-thread traffic;
+they do not change who can read durable channel history.
+
+`fanout_policy` accepts:
+
+- `capability_match` to select a small capability/text-matched peer set
+- `coordinator` to route unaddressed traffic to one named peer
+- `all_members` to deliver unaddressed traffic to every eligible local member
+
+Update the policy with `agh network channels update` or the Network UI. Use `coordinator` only when
+one peer is responsible for triage; use `capability_match` for general collaboration where the
+runtime should avoid prompting every local session.
+
